llator model is Microfreak/UI/Oscillator/Knob/Type/Harmo.",["Content (Harmo)"]],["p-d2f2adb88cbb1370.html","source-block-253","The Wave knob morphs through different tables of harmonic amplitudes and switches between them. Higher values provide tones with richer harmonic content.",["Content (Harmo)"]],["p-d2f2adb88cbb1370.html","source-block-410","Source",["Content (Harmo)"]],["p-d2f2adb88cbb1370.html","source-block-423","Microfreak/UG/06 Dig Osc/03 Types/04 Harmo",["Content (Harmo)","Source"]],["p-476b3c9493122fc8.html","source-block-104","Sculpting (Harmo)",[]],["p-476b3c9493122fc8.html","source-block-126","Set by the Microfreak/UI/Oscillator/Knob/Timbre while the oscillator model is Microfreak/UI/Oscillator/Knob/Type/Harmo.",["Sculpting (Harmo)"]],["p-476b3c9493122fc8.html","source-block-257","The Timbre knob morphs between a sine and a triangle wave. A harmonic derived from a sine wave sounds different from one built from a triangle wave.",["Sculpting (Harmo)"]],["p-476b3c9493122fc8.html","source-block-409","Source",["Sculpting (Harmo)"]],["p-476b3c9493122fc8.html","source-block-422","Microfreak/UG/06 Dig Osc/03 Types/04 Harmo",["Sculpting (Harmo)","Source"]],["p-42e05e9de3033684.html","source-block-211","Hit grains",[]],["p-42e05e9de3033684.html","source-block-226","Oscillator model 21 of 22 on the Microfreak/UI/Oscillator/Knob/Type, shown on the display as Hit grains.",["Hit grains"]],["p-42e05e9de3033684.html","source-block-338","Parameters",["Hit grains"]],["p-42e05e9de3033684.html","source-block-355","Microfreak/UI/Oscillator/Knob/Wave → Microfreak/UI/Oscillator/Knob/Type/Hit Grains/Start",["Hit grains","Parameters"]],["p-42e05e9de3033684.html","source-block-458","Microfreak/UI/Oscillator/Knob/Timbre → Microfreak/UI/Oscillator/Knob/Type/Hit Grains/Density",["Hit grains","Parameters"]],["p-42e05e9de3033684.html","source-block-565","Microfreak/UI/Oscillator/Knob/Shape → Microfreak/UI/Oscillator/Knob/Type/Hit Grains/Shape",["Hit grains","Parameters"]],["p-42e0